From: Micheal Waltz <micheal@ecliptik.com>
Date: Tue, 12 May 2026 10:09:52 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] dos: Phase 11 patch 0057 -- Shape D mixer-flag silence-detect
 (SDL reader)

SDL3-DOS side of the Shape D mixer-flag silence-detect fps lever for
wave-36 PLAY6. Pairs with patches/SDL_mixer/0001 (the writer) to
replace SDL/0054 Shape A's bytewise post-mix scan with an O(1)
volatile-int load.

User direction 2026-05-12 (no_playing_it_safe.md): "We don't make
Cave Story great on DOS by playing it safe." Wave-36 picks Shape D
(architectural change; aggressive ceiling) over Shape E (cheaper-
scan-loop; safe ceiling) per team-lead pivot. Risk-honest framing:
mechanism IS architecturally correct (SDL_mixer's
`mixer->actual_mixed_bytes` is the source-of-truth for "did the mix
produce non-silence"; the bytewise scan was redundant); killswitch
hygiene per correctness_vs_perf_trade_machinery_at_authoring.md;
PLAY6 measures real-HW trade; wave-37+ flips ship-default if data
clears.

Mechanism:

  - New static `g_dos_silence_shape_d_active` resolved at OpenDevice
    from `SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_SILENCE_SHAPE=D` (strict-"D" match per
    CLAUDE.md env-var convention). Default false (Shape A path active;
    identical to wave-35 SDL/0054 ship behavior). Any value other than
    literal single-char "D" (unset, "A", "E", lowercase "d", anything)
    falls through to Shape A.

  - PlayDevice silence-detect block dispatches on the active shape:
        if (g_dos_silence_shape_d_active) {
            all_silence = (doskutsu_mixer_actual_mixed_bytes == 0);
        } else {
            /* Shape A bytewise scan; unchanged from SDL/0054 */
        }
    The remaining silence-skip + ring-write + audio_thread bracket
    paths are unchanged: only the silence detection itself swaps
    mechanism.

  - Weak-fallback definition of `doskutsu_mixer_actual_mixed_bytes`
    in this TU (default 0; SDL_mixer's strong definition from
    patches/SDL_mixer/0001 overrides at final link). Lets SDL3's own
    test/utility binaries (which link libSDL3.a only without
    libSDL3_mixer.a) link cleanly even though they never engage
    Shape D at runtime -- the weak default reads as 0 (silent), and
    no SDL3 test binary exercises the DOS audio backend.

  - Boot banner emits one of FOUR variants per flush-instr's wave-36
    contract section 3.4 (engagement-verify gate via doskutsu_dbg_log):

      Variant 1 (Shape A default):
        "audio: SDL/0054 silence-detect Shape A active
         (default; bytewise scan; SFX-correct)"
      Variant 2 (Shape D engaged):
        "audio: SDL/0054 silence-detect Shape D active
         (SHAPE=D; mixer-flag fast-path via
         doskutsu_mixer_actual_mixed_bytes; replaces Shape A
         bytewise scan with O(1) volatile load)"
      Variant 3 (Shape A killswitched via SDL/0056):
        "audio: SDL/0054 silence-detect DISABLED
         (env-var; perf-experiment)"
      Variant 4 (conflict: SILENCE_DETECT=0 + SHAPE=D both set):
        "audio: SDL/0054 silence-detect DISABLED
         (SILENCE_DETECT=0 overrides SILENCE_SHAPE=D)"

    Operator BAT cell that sets SHAPE=D MUST produce variant 2 in
    SDLDBG.LOG; absence of variant 2 means the gate chain didn't
    engage and the fps measurement is invalid (per
    contract_grep_targets_require_enabling_env_vars.md the
    wave-35 PLAY5 trap that bit nx 0131 / SDL/0055 instrumentation).

Conflict resolution (variant 4): SILENCE_DETECT=0 (entire silence-
detect path disabled) WINS over SHAPE=D (mechanism pick within the
silence-detect path). When both env vars are set, the silence-detect
dispatch block is entirely skipped, so the Shape pick is moot. Banner
variant 4 makes the conflict visible to log capture.

Cost trade (predicted; framed as hypothesis per
perf_predictions_unreliable.md):
  Shape A: bytewise scan of 256-4096 buffer bytes per audio-thread
           iter; cost dominated by cooperative-scheduler interaction
           during the wall-clock window the scan runs (per
           PHASE11-WAVE-35-FINDINGS section 2.1; +3.34 ms fi_ms slice
           regression wave-35 vs wave-34).
  Shape D: single volatile-int load (~0 ns at -O3). The scheduling-
           window the load occupies is sub-microsecond; no
           cooperative-yield opportunity.

PLAY6 prediction band: +3 to +5 fps recovery from 35.71 baseline (full
~3.34 ms fi_ms recovery to ~39-40 fps target). Real-HW measurement
settles cost; if PLAY6 == PLAY1 (no fps gain), the wave-35 cost
attribution hypothesis was wrong (scan-loop wall-clock wasn't the
driver) and the real cost lives elsewhere; SDL/0058's mechanism
histogram backstop reveals where for wave-37 picks.

SFX-correctness gate: the mixer's actual_mixed_bytes captures track-
output-stream byte counts; when a Pixtone SFX fires via MIX_PlayTrack,
the track's TrackGetCallback puts non-zero data into the per-track
output_stream during MixerCallback, mixer->actual_mixed_bytes
increments, Shape D PlayDevice takes the audible-write path, ring
write happens, SFX plays. Same correctness profile as Shape A; the
difference is HOW we detected non-silence (mixer bookkeeping vs scan),
not WHETHER we wrote the audible buffer.

If operator reports SFX silent in PLAY6 but audible in PLAY1 (Shape
A baseline), that's an attribution bug in actual_mixed_bytes tracking
(very unlikely; SDL3_mixer's own tests rely on this counter being
correct) and we revert Shape D as a ship-default candidate; the
SHAPE=A default path remains the wave-36 ship binary's default
regardless.

Concurrency / atomicity:

  - Writer (SDL_mixer/0001): MixerCallback writes the value at the
    end of its body, just before SDL_PutAudioStreamData.
    MixerCallback runs on the audio thread under device->lock per
    SDL3 audio core's SDL_PlaybackAudioThreadIterate at
    SDL_audio.c:1179-1289.
  - Reader (this patch): PlayDevice reads the value in the silence-
    detect dispatch block. PlayDevice runs on the SAME audio thread
    under the SAME device->lock as MixerCallback (SDL3 calls
    GetDeviceBuf -> mix loop -> PlayDevice in one critical
    section).
  - Therefore: same-thread reader; no cross-thread atomicity
    question. `volatile` for compiler-fence semantics only. Same
    pattern as the existing `doskutsu_audio_irq_count` /
    `doskutsu_audio_irq_wall_us` volatile exports from SDL3-DOS.

Workspace-local DOS-port patch per memory/sdl_ai_policy.md; never
upstreamed.

Validation:
  - Compile clean at i486 -O3.
  - Symbol `_doskutsu_mixer_actual_mixed_bytes` weak in libSDL3.a;
    strong in libSDL3_mixer.a; final-link resolution verified.
  - All 4 banner variants verified in libSDL3.a via
    `strings | grep "Shape [AD]\\|SILENCE_DETECT=0 overrides"`.
  - SDL3 test binaries link clean (weak fallback resolves).

Coexistence with the patch family:
  - SDL/0050 -- DOS GetDeviceBuf quiescence gate (superseded by
                SDL/0054 mechanism; killswitch hint name retained;
                orthogonal to SHAPE=D)
  - SDL/0053 -- engine-signaled pre-shutdown gate disable (still
                gates the silence-detect block via
                g_dos_audio_quiescence_gate_disabled; same code path
                under Shape D as Shape A)
  - SDL/0054 -- Shape A silent-Pixtone-SFX fix (this patch's
                fallback; remains default-ON; PlayDevice's silence-
                detect dispatch lands here when SHAPE != "D")
  - SDL/0055 -- P12 SDL-side audio brackets (independent
                instrumentation; gates separately; coexists trivially)
  - SDL/0056 -- silence-detect runtime killswitch (entirely disables
                the silence-detect block when SILENCE_DETECT=0;
                takes precedence over SHAPE=D per variant 4 banner)
  - SDL_mixer/0001 -- Shape D mixer-flag writer (paired patch; this
                       patch is its reader)
  - SDL/0058 -- Shape A mechanism histogram (planned ride-along;
                pure SDL-side; gates separately on
                SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_SILENCE_HISTO=1)

Cross-reference:
  - docs/PHASE11-WAVE-36-CONTRACT.md section 4 + 5.7 (PLAY6 Shape D
    fps lever; predicted +3 to +5 fps; refutation discriminator
    boot-banner variant 2 in SDLDBG.LOG)
  - docs/PHASE11-WAVE-35-FINDINGS.md section 2 (the +3.34 ms fi_ms
    slice regression Shape D aims to recover)
  - patches/SDL_mixer/0001-shape-d-mixer-flag-silence-detect-setter.patch
    (the writer; defines `doskutsu_mixer_actual_mixed_bytes` strong)
  - memory/no_playing_it_safe.md (user directive 2026-05-12: prefer
    biggest correctness-retaining ceiling over smallest LOC)
  - memory/correctness_vs_perf_trade_machinery_at_authoring.md
    (killswitch hygiene; ship default-OFF; PLAY6 confirms; wave-37
    flips default if data clears)
  - memory/contract_grep_targets_require_enabling_env_vars.md
    (banner-variant-2 grep target is essential for PLAY6
    engagement-verify)
  - memory/perf_predictions_unreliable.md (PLAY6 prediction band
    framed as hypothesis; measurement settles)
