+/* DOSKUTSU patch (Phase 11 patch 0057): Shape D mixer-flag silence-
+   detect engagement state. Default false (Shape A bytewise-scan path
+   runs; identical to wave-35 SDL/0054 ship behavior). Set
+   SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_SILENCE_SHAPE=D at SDL_Init time to engage Shape
+   D: PlayDevice reads the `doskutsu_mixer_actual_mixed_bytes`
+   volatile (defined in SDL3_mixer's MixerCallback per
+   patches/SDL_mixer/0001) instead of bytewise-scanning the staging
+   buffer. Strict-"D" match (single char + null terminator); any
+   other value (unset, "A", "E", lowercase "d", anything) falls
+   through to Shape A.
+
+   Architectural argument: SDL3_mixer's `mixer->actual_mixed_bytes`
+   is the source-of-truth for "did this iter produce non-silence"
+   (it's the max group_bytes across all groups' track output
+   streams, set at SDL_mixer.c line 619-621). The post-mix bytewise
+   scan that Shape A performs is a redundant re-verification of
+   what the mixer already knew. Shape D eliminates the redundancy:
+   one volatile-int load replaces N bytes of compare loop.
+
+   Hot-path cost trade:
+     Shape A: bytewise scan of 256-4096 staging buffer bytes,
+              early-exit on first non-silence byte. Cost dominated
+              by cooperative-scheduler interaction during the
+              wall-clock window the scan runs (per
+              docs/PHASE11-WAVE-35-FINDINGS.md section 2.1; +3.34 ms
+              fi_ms slice regression measured wave-35 vs wave-34).
+     Shape D: single volatile-int load (`*p` where p points at the
+              SDL_mixer-side global). Cost ~0 ns. The scheduling-
+              window the load occupies is sub-microsecond; no
+              cooperative-yield opportunity.
+
+   Per memory/no_playing_it_safe.md (user directive 2026-05-12):
+   "we don't make Cave Story great on DOS by playing it safe."
+   Shape D is the aggressive-but-architecturally-correct shape;
+   Shape E (smaller-scan-window variant in nx 0058's histogram
+   backstop framing) is the safe fallback if Shape D surfaces
+   correctness issues in real-HW PLAY6.
+
+   Conflict with g_dos_silence_detect_enabled (SDL/0056): if
+   SILENCE_DETECT=0 (silence-detect entirely disabled) AND SHAPE=D
+   are both set, SILENCE_DETECT=0 WINS (no silence-detect path runs;
+   Shape pick is moot because the silence-detect dispatch block
+   doesn't execute). Boot banner emits variant 4 to make the
+   conflict visible to log capture.
+
+   Wave-36 PLAY6 engagement matrix:
+     PLAY1/2/3/4/5/8/9: SHAPE unset -> Shape A active (default;
+                       baseline + audio decomp variations)
+     PLAY6:            SHAPE=D set -> Shape D active (this patch's
+                       fps lever; predicted +3 to +5 fps vs PLAY1) */
+static bool g_dos_silence_shape_d_active = false;
+
+/* DOSKUTSU patch (Phase 11 patch 0057): weak-fallback definition for
+   the SDL_mixer-defined volatile. The strong definition lives in
+   SDL3_mixer's MixerCallback TU
+   (vendor/SDL_mixer/src/SDL_mixer.c, file-scope after MixerCallback)
+   per patches/SDL_mixer/0001 -- when SDL3-DOS is linked into a binary
+   that ALSO links libSDL3_mixer.a (the doskutsu.exe link order), the
+   strong def from SDL_mixer wins at link time and MixerCallback's
+   writes are observable here.
+
+   The `__attribute__((weak))` default-zero definition exists to keep
+   SDL3's own test/utility binaries (which link libSDL3.a only without
+   libSDL3_mixer.a) link-clean: those binaries never engage Shape D
+   (no MixerCallback to set the value; SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_SILENCE_SHAPE
+   is never set in them), but the SDL_dosaudio_sb.c TU still contains
+   the read instruction in the Shape D code path that's compiled in.
+   Weak default-zero means: read returns 0 (silent) ALWAYS in those
+   builds; the Shape D path becomes equivalent to "always treat as
+   silent" -- which is HARMLESS because none of SDL3's test binaries
+   exercise the DOS audio backend at runtime.
+
+   Concurrency: same-thread reader (audio thread under device->lock
+   during PlaybackAudioThreadIterate); same thread is also the writer
+   (MixerCallback runs inside the same PlaybackAudioThreadIterate
+   critical section). No cross-thread sync required; `volatile` for
+   compiler-fence semantics only.
+
+   Per memory/no_playing_it_safe.md aggressive-but-not-reckless
+   framing: the weak fallback is the "not reckless" half -- it
+   ensures the architectural change doesn't break unrelated SDL3
+   test infrastructure on the way to delivering the Shape D fps
+   lever for doskutsu.exe. */
+volatile int doskutsu_mixer_actual_mixed_bytes __attribute__((weak)) = 0;
+
